-- title:
--   Noetherian stalk, A-residues and chart density at supersingular points
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes, $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$, and let $K\subseteq L((X))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb Q\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$, and $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion $j(\mathsf q)$. Form the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X$, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures `chartAlgFin` of $A[j]$ and `chartAlgInf` of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$. Let $z\in\mathfrak X$ be such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under $\mathfrak X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ lies in $\mathfrak m_z$, and let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin})$ map to $z$ under $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, with $y$ supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has trivial $q$-torsion. Then, writing $\mathcal O=\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ and $\mathrm{germ}_y:\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\to\mathcal O$ for the germ map through $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$: $\mathcal O$ is Noetherian; every $r\in\mathcal O$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_z$ to the germ of some $a\in A$; for every $r\in\mathcal O$ and every $n$ there is $c$ in `chartAlgFin` with $r-\mathrm{germ}_y(c)\in\mathfrak m_z^{\,n}$; and $\mathrm{germ}_y(c)\in\mathfrak m_z$ if and only if $c$ lies in the prime of $y$.
--
--   This is the local structure statement at a supersingular closed point of the two-chart integral model over $A$ of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, in the auxiliary level with a guard prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$: the stalk is Noetherian, its residue field is generated by the residue field of $A$, the finite chart algebra is dense for the $\mathfrak m_z$-adic filtration, and membership in $\mathfrak m_z$ detects the prime of $y$. It supports the later analysis of Drinfeld chart witnesses and of the semilinear inertia action at $q$ at this auxiliary level.
